{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And He gave El (to Moses)</b> — in gematria: this is the Talmud." "<b>When He finished</b> — written defective. Just as a bride is adorned with 24 adornments enumerated in Isaiah, so too a Torah scholar must be adorned with 24 books." "<b>Two tablets</b> — corresponding to heaven and earth, bridegroom and bride, two Torahs, and two worlds." "<b>Tablets</b> — for those who weary their jaws (לחי). לחת in א״ת ב״ש = כס״א, teaching that they were taken from the Throne of Glory."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {3 "ע\"ש שיגעים בלחי: read as עַל שֶׁיָּגִיעַם בַּלַּחַי, 'for those who weary their jaws' — a wordplay on לחת (tablets) and לחי (jaw). The phrase appears corrupt or abbreviated in the witness; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:53.922466289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}